{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-brings-riemann-hurwitz","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:brings-riemann-hurwitz","kind":"lemma","title":"Riemann--Hurwitz count for the canonical map $\\Sigma_4 \\to \\mathbb{P}(V)$","proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-brings-riemann-hurwitz"],"tags":["riemann-hurwitz","ramification","brings-surface","s5-symmetry"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.brings_riemann_hurwitz","text":"brings-riemann-hurwitz.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:brings-riemann-hurwitz\"></a><p><em>The Reeb quotient <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M_S \\to \\Sigma_4</code> collapses <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{U}(1)</code>-orbits to the weight-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code> subalgebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_0 = A^{\\mathrm{U}(1)}</code>. The canonical covering <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi \\colon \\Sigma_4 \\to \\mathbb{P}(V)</code> has degree <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4</code> with total ramification</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  R_{\\mathrm{tot}}\n  = 2g(\\Sigma_4) - 2 - 4(2g(\\mathbb{P}^1) - 2)\n  = 14.</code></pre>\n<p><em>This ramification is distributed by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S_5</code>-symmetry over exactly <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">6</code> branch points.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-riemann-hurwitz.md","heading":"Lemma","number":"7.4.12"}
